Impact:
According to Decision of the Board of the Eurasian Economic Commission dated April 21, 2015 No. 30 “On non-tariff regulation measures” (hereinafter referred to as the Decision) established the permitting procedure for the import into the customs territory of the EAEU of goods (Appendix No. 2 to the Decision). The licensing procedures are applied to the importation of certain digital goods to the Eurasian Economic Union, including Russia. These digital goods are the following: (i) Civil radio-electronic equipment and/or high-frequency devices including those which are built-in or form a part of other goods; (ii) Special hardware meant for secret information acquisition; (iii) Encryption devices.

Specifically, 2.16 “Radio-electronic equipment and (or ) high-frequency devices for civil purposes, including those built-in or included in other goods,” the import of which into the customs territory of the EAEU is carried out in accordance with the Regulations on the import into the customs territory of the Eurasian Economic Union of radio-electronic devices and high-frequency devices for civil purposes, including built-in or included in other goods (Appendix No. 15 to the Decision) when submitting to the customs authority of a member state of the EAEU a license from the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Russia or a conclusion (permit document) of Roskomnadzor or information on the inclusion of radio-electronic equipment and high-frequency devices in the unified register of radio-electronic equipment and high-frequency devices; 
2.17 “Special technical means intended for secretly obtaining information”, the import of which into the customs territory of the EAEU is carried out in accordance with the Regulations on the import into the customs territory of the Eurasian Economic Union and export from the customs territory of the Eurasian Economic Union of special technical means intended for secretly obtaining information ( Appendix No. 16 to the Decision) when submitting to the customs authority a license from the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Russia and (or) a conclusion (permit document) from  Federal Security Service; 
2.19. “Encryption (cryptographic) means”, the import of which into the customs territory of the EAEU is carried out in accordance with the Regulations on the import into the customs territory of the Eurasian Economic Union and export from the customs territory of the Eurasian Economic Union of encryption (cryptographic) means (Appendix No. 9 to the Decision) upon presentation to the customs authority of a member state of the EAEU if there is information about the inclusion of the corresponding notification in the unified register of notifications or if there is a license from the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Russia and (or) a conclusion (permit document).
